WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.600
The public didn't buy the Biden administration and&nbsp;
the Federal Reserve's claims that inflation was

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:14.960
likely transitory. Concern about increasing prices&nbsp;
has been percolating in the polls for months

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.401
and it is having a powerful effect on the&nbsp;
president's ratings. In the Harvard/Harris&nbsp;poll

00:00:19.401 --> 00:00:24.800
from November 2021, Biden's approval rating&nbsp;
on handling the economy dropped 20 points since

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:32.160
his inauguration, from 61 to 41%. Less than half,&nbsp;
45%, expressed confidence in the administration,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:38.000
and separately in the Fed, to keep inflation at&nbsp;bay.
In the mid-November Wall Street Journal poll,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.880
registered voters gave Republicans in Congress&nbsp;
an 18-point lead over the Democrats on being

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:49.040
better able to get inflation under control. As for&nbsp;
the effect inflation is having on Americans,

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.800
19% in the December Monmouth University poll&nbsp;
said that they cut back a lot, and 21% a little,

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:01.840
on holiday gifts because of high prices. 34% have&nbsp;
experienced more shipping delays than in the past,

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.995
and 46% of experienced items being out of stock.

00:01:06.995 --> 00:01:13.438
Did you have trouble buying a holiday gift? Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know what other topics you'd like

00:01:13.438 --> 00:01:21.000
our scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and&nbsp;
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

